       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. V59SORTKEY.
      *> V59 - A NUMERIC SORT KEY COMPARES BY ALGEBRAIC VALUE, WHATEVER
      *> ITS REPRESENTATION. ISO/IEC 1989:2023 14.9.40.4 GR19 SENDS A
      *> NUMERIC KEY TO 8.8.4.2.4, WHICH COMPARES ALGEBRAIC VALUES "WITH
      *> REGARD TO THE ALGEBRAIC VALUE OF THE OPERANDS" AND IS EXPLICITLY
      *> INDEPENDENT OF USAGE. THE KEY WINDOW OF THE SORT RECORD NOW
      *> HOLDS THE ITEM'S TRUE BYTES (13.18.60.4 GR4, RADIX 2, TWO'S
      *> COMPLEMENT), SO A NEGATIVE KEY'S FIRST BYTE IS 0xFF - SORTING
      *> THOSE BYTES AS TEXT WOULD PUT EVERY NEGATIVE KEY LAST. THE
      *> RUNTIME DECODES THE WINDOW THROUGH THE KEY ITEM'S OWN PROFILE.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT SWK ASSIGN TO "v59-sort-wk.dat".
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       SD SWK.
       01 SW-REC.
          05 SW-KEY PIC S9(4) COMP.
          05 SW-TAG PIC X(3).
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 DONE-FLAG PIC X VALUE "N".
       01 IX PIC 9 VALUE 0.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           SORT SWK ON ASCENDING KEY SW-KEY
               INPUT PROCEDURE IS FEED
               OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS DRAIN
           STOP RUN.
       FEED.
      *> RELEASED OUT OF ORDER, WITH NEGATIVES ON BOTH SIDES OF ZERO.
           MOVE 1000 TO SW-KEY
           MOVE "BIG" TO SW-TAG
           RELEASE SW-REC
           MOVE -50 TO SW-KEY
           MOVE "NEG" TO SW-TAG
           RELEASE SW-REC
           MOVE 7 TO SW-KEY
           MOVE "SML" TO SW-TAG
           RELEASE SW-REC
           MOVE -3 TO SW-KEY
           MOVE "NHI" TO SW-TAG
           RELEASE SW-REC
           MOVE 0 TO SW-KEY
           MOVE "ZER" TO SW-TAG
           RELEASE SW-REC.
       DRAIN.
      *> ASCENDING ALGEBRAIC ORDER: -50, -3, 0, 7, 1000.
           PERFORM UNTIL DONE-FLAG = "Y"
               RETURN SWK RECORD
                   AT END MOVE "Y" TO DONE-FLAG
                   NOT AT END DISPLAY SW-TAG " " SW-KEY
               END-RETURN
           END-PERFORM.
